 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Ask locals, especially those who cook. Asking in a restaurant can give you a good idea of the cafe scene, while asking cooks puts you in the ballpark price wise. Social media is also useful. Check out the local foodie pages and see where people are raving about what. Then it' you versus the crowd. Do you want something busy and restauranty, or a quieter, more homely experience? Small towns love their pubs. They often do real food, and the staff will usually know the best bits.",
